@page
@model AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About This Project";
}

<div class="container mt-4">

    <h1 class="mb-3">HCAMiniEHR – Mini Electronic Health Record System</h1>

    <p class="text-muted">
        This project is developed as part of an academic capstone assignment to demonstrate
        real-world application of ASP.NET Core, Entity Framework Core, LINQ, SQL Server,
        and Git-based collaboration.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h4>📌 Project Overview</h4>
    <p>
        HCAMiniEHR is a simplified Electronic Health Record (EHR) system designed to manage
        core healthcare workflows such as patient registration, appointment scheduling,
        and laboratory order management. The application follows real hospital business
        rules and clean architectural practices.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h4>🛠 Technology Stack</h4>
    <ul>
        <li><b>Framework:</b> ASP.NET Core Razor Pages (.NET 8)</li>
        <li><b>ORM:</b> Entity Framework Core</li>
        <li><b>Database:</b> SQL Server</li>
        <li><b>Querying:</b> LINQ</li>
        <li><b>Architecture:</b> Repository + Service Pattern</li>
        <li><b>UI:</b> Bootstrap (Responsive Design)</li>
        <li><b>Version Control:</b> Git & GitHub</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h4>🏥 Core Functional Modules</h4>

    <h6>1️⃣ Patient Management</h6>
    <ul>
        <li>Create, View, Edit, and Delete patient records</li>
        <li>Validation for DOB, mobile number, and required fields</li>
        <li>Patient lifecycle management</li>
    </ul>

    <h6>2️⃣ Appointment Management</h6>
    <ul>
        <li>Schedule appointments for patients</li>
        <li>Assign doctors to appointments</li>
        <li>Business rule: Doctor availability based on daily appointment limit</li>
        <li>Appointment lifecycle: Scheduled → Completed / Cancelled</li>
        <li>Stored procedures used for appointment creation and status updates</li>
    </ul>

    <h6>3️⃣ Lab Order Management</h6>
    <ul>
        <li>Create lab orders only after appointment completion</li>
        <li>Track lab order status (Pending → Completed)</li>
        <li>Stored procedures used for lab order creation and updates</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h4>📊 Reporting & Analytics (LINQ)</h4>
    <p>
        The system includes analytical reports implemented using LINQ queries:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Pending Lab Orders Report</li>
        <li>Patients Without Follow-Up Appointments</li>
        <li>Doctor Productivity Report (appointments count per doctor)</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h4>📈 Dashboard</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>Total Patients Count</li>
        <li>Total Appointments</li>
        <li>Today’s Appointments</li>
        <li>Pending Lab Orders</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The dashboard provides a quick operational overview of the healthcare system.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h4>🔐 Security & Validation</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>Model-level validation using Data Annotations and IValidatableObject</li>
        <li>Business rule enforcement in service layer</li>
        <li>Authentication support using ASP.NET Core Identity (optional enhancement)</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h4>🧱 Architecture & Design Principles</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>Separation of concerns (UI, Service, Repository, Data)</li>
        <li>DTOs used for reporting and dashboard data transfer</li>
        <li>Stored Procedures used for critical database operations</li>
        <li>Audit logging implemented using SQL triggers</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h4>🔄 Git & Collaboration</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>Multiple branches used for feature development</li>
        <li>Meaningful commits with clear messages</li>
        <li>Pull Requests used for merging features into main branch</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        🔗 <b>GitHub Repository:</b><br />
        <a href="https://github.com/0mkar303/HCAMiniEHR.git" target="_blank">
            Git Repository Link
        </a>
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h4>🎯 Learning Outcomes</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>Hands-on experience with full-stack ASP.NET Core development</li>
        <li>Practical understanding of healthcare business workflows</li>
        <li>Strong understanding of LINQ, EF Core, and SQL integration</li>
        <li>Real-world application of Git and collaborative development</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <p class="text-muted">
        This project demonstrates the practical application of enterprise-level
        software development concepts in a healthcare domain.
    </p>

</div>
